Find all positive integers \( n \) for which there exists a function \( f : \mathbb{Z}^+ \to \mathbb{Z}^+ \) such that:
1. \( f(1) = n \);
2. For all positive integers \( k \) and \( m \), if \( f(k) = m \), then \( f(m) = f(k+m) - f(k) \);
3. There exists at least one positive integer \( k \) such that \( f(k+19) \neq f(k) + 19 \).

Find the smallest positive integer \( n \) such that there exist positive integers \( a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n \) with the following properties:
1. \( a_1 < a_2 < \cdots < a_n \);
2. The product \( a_1 \cdot a_2 \cdots a_n \) is divisible by 2007 but the product of any \( k < n \) of these numbers is not divisible by 2007.

Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{aligned} 3x+5 &\quad \text{ if } x \le 1, \\
ax+b &\quad \text{ if } x > 1.
\end{aligned}
\right.\]Find [a,] and [b](/usr) such that [f](/usr) is a continuous function.

Alice has a magical machine that takes a number \( x \) and outputs a number \( f(x) \) following the rule: 
\[ f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x + 3 & \text{if } x \text{ is odd}, \\
\frac{x}{2} & \text{if } x \text{ is even}.
\end{array}
\right. \]
She starts with the number \( 2023 \) and applies \( f \) repeatedly until she reaches \( 1 \). Each operation she performs on the number is called a step. After reaching \( 1 \), she continues applying \( f \) to \( 1 \) until she cycles back to \( 1 \). How many total steps does Alice perform before she completes this cycle?

A mathematical function \( f(x) \) is defined for all real numbers \( x \) as follows:
\[ f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
\frac{1}{2} x^3 - 2x^2 + 3x - 4 & \text{if } x \leq 0, \\
\frac{1}{4} x^4 - x^3 + 3x^2 - 4x + 5 & \text{if } x > 0.
\end{array}
\right. \]
Find the value(s) of \( x \) at which the function \( f(x) \) has a local minimum, and determine whether any of these are also global minima. Provide a detailed justification for your answers.
